  // Realms and cultures (CAMPAIGN_OVERHAUL.md 4.1). A realm's culture decides what its villages raise and which lines its lords
  // promote along; "lines" are the troop each role fields at tiers I-VII (each entry must be an upgrade of the one before, or
  // the same troop). Troops carry their culture in troops.json; "common" troops are open to every culture.
  // A realm's "home" is where its land grows from on a new map ([x, z] from -1 to 1; -1 z is the north) and "reach" lets
  // it grow further (map units on the original map) before its neighbours stop it (docs/WORLD.md W1). "relations" are the
  // wars and truces a new campaign opens with; realms not listed start at peace. A culture's "kin" are the cultures whose
  // troops its lines may borrow (and its men may train as); the four realms of docs/WORLD.md W3 field their own troops in
  // two roles and borrow the other two.
